    "interpretation": [
      "Zero fallback across445342view requests and35156fused openings confirms real ordinary-workload coverage. The result is not a failed activation.",
      "Avoided intermediate normalization reduces resolver-created nodes28.4%, but total nodes only5.9%. Invariant branches still materialize at the unchanged solver boundary. Unifier resolver visits rise14.6%.",
      "Pure admission adds2220916entries, ordered validation1741375entries and fused opening116278entries. These replace less resolver work than they introduce traversal; they are not equal-cost CPU units.",
      "Only44352rounded pooled live bytes are saved. sessionHeap observes small-allocation slab classes only; directly mapped large allocations and other process mappings are excluded. Peak RSS grows in these controls.",
      "Normalization node counters are inclusive attribution; existing resolve/open families overlap. Do not sum them into allocations or CPU. Admission counts type visits, row-history hops and labels, while validation/open counters are separate walk entries."
    ]
